# Hummingbird-scoped presets (delivered by 92-variant-customizations.sh).
#
# The Hummingbird base has no desktop. Its 90-default.preset is trimmed for
# servers and names no display manager, and 99-default-disable.preset ends
# with `disable *`. On first boot systemd applies preset policy and removes
# the enablement that the build made for any unit that no preset names.
#
# Measured on the boot gate of run 43868943848 (hummingbird:tuna), on a
# pass that ended in a login prompt on the console and no graphical session:
#
#   [ 8.689713] systemd[1]: Applying preset policy.
#   [ 8.785223] systemd[1]: Removed '.../graphical.target.wants/gdm.service'.
#   [ 8.785701] systemd[1]: Removed '.../display-manager.service'.
#
# graphical.target only Wants=display-manager.service, so with that alias
# gone the target is reached with no display manager behind it. Nothing
# started gdm, tunaos-desktop-contract.service never ran, and the Gate
# waited 900 seconds for TUNAOS_DESKTOP_CONTRACT_OK.
#
# This names gdm so the first boot keeps what the build intended. It is
# scoped to hummingbird, so no other variant changes its first-boot policy.
# A preset only affects units that are installed. The greetd flavors mask
# gdm (greetd-system-integration.sh), and systemd ignores a masked unit.
enable gdm.service
